bejoin_mipspic_O2.so, bejoin_mipsunal -- MIPS32 big-endian images for the
caller evidence of option bejoin callers through PIC calls and past
unaligned loads (GH-904; tests/stages/kuna-bejoin-mipspic.xml).

What they are
  bejoin_mipspic_O2.so  o32 PIC shared object from bejoin_mipspic.c: every
                        call is lw $25,%call16(f)($28); jalr $25, and c_unal
                        loads an unaligned word into $3 right after a call.
  bejoin_mipsunal       static non-PIC executable from bejoin_mipsunal.S:
                        add_hi leaves a carry in $3, c_unal reads an
                        unaligned word into $3 (lwl/lwr) after jal add_hi.

Why they are vendored
  CI has no MIPS toolchain, and the assertions depend on the exact
  instructions and register choices.

Where they came from
  Debian mips-linux-gnu-gcc 12.2.0-14 (docker) and Ubuntu
  mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc 10.3.0 and its binutils (host, -EB):

      mips-linux-gnu-gcc -O2 -fPIC -shared -nostdlib -Wl,--build-id=none \
          bejoin_mipspic.c -o bejoin_mipspic_O2.so
      mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc -EB -mno-abicalls -fno-pic -c bejoin_mipsunal.S -o unal.o
      mipsel-linux-gnu-ld -EB -static -nostdlib -e c_low --build-id=none unal.o \
          -o bejoin_mipsunal

  sha256:
    9631b19d4499470a62d043e8b2fd88d02620499561b7f8c01447e43fdf1b4098  bejoin_mipspic_O2.so
